Subject: Profile A records: own, add and other counts per site, and the own-read hit takes the bytecode

What this does
  - The profile writer emits `A <digest> site=<n> pc=<pc> own= add= other= nown= nxf= [o<i>=shape:slot:count] [x<i>=pre:post:slot:count] rest=` per property-write site and `R` lines for reads, counting own-slot writes, adding transitions and other kinds separately, with the shapes seen.
  - regvm_own_read_hit takes the bytecode, so the read-side records are attributed to the right profile slot; the seven call sites in quickjs-regvm-step.inc pass it.

Why we need it
  The S sample of a write site mixes adds and own writes; the generator needs the split to pick transition stores, uncached stores and own shapes.

Soundness
  Profile output only; execution is unchanged when no profile is requested.

Failure modes
  A reader of the profile that does not know A or R lines skips them.

